WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.160
I'm not recommending
you cut school

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.230
to go to trunk shows
or fashion shows.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.930
But I did a little bit of
that when I was younger too.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:10.620
By sharing what I
know, I hope that it

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.689
will inspire you to create
and express yourself

00:00:13.689 --> 00:00:14.355
through fashion.

00:00:14.355 --> 00:00:15.970
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:19.164
My grandmother would buy me
Vogue, French Vogue sometimes

00:00:19.164 --> 00:00:20.080
if I was really lucky.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.000
And I would just pour
over these images.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.240
That was my first
introduction to fashion.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.170
I'll be discussing things that
I wish I knew starting out.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.440
The heart of my class is
sharing the technical process.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.080
Once in a while it's a fabric
that inspires the dress.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.310
And other times
it's the dress we

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.800
want to make that
inspires the fabric.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:47.030
This is called intarsia when
the fabric is not appliqued.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:50.550
It is actually pieced together,
almost like a jigsaw puzzle.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:54.180
A nice juxtaposition, of
finishing something beautifully

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.520
and then leaving edges
of the fabric frayed.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.560
The runway show is
very important to me.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:06.370
You can transmit not only ideas
about texture and proportion

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:08.850
but also about
spirit and emotion.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:13.246
I was brought into Louis
Vuitton to shake things up.

00:01:13.946 --> 00:01:15.820
And it didn't always
sit well with the people

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:16.930
who were there before me.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.450
A lot of the ideas that I
had early on I was told,

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.220
you can't put this
on the runway.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:23.830
And it really was when I
stopped listening to everybody

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:26.110
and did what I thought
was right that I did

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:27.460
what I was brought in to do.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:30.430
But I personally feel
good when I take a risk.

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:32.650
I'm proud of myself
when I take a chance.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:33.680
I think you should too.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.640
I hope you learn
fashion is not an art.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.510
It's part of the art of living.

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:41.530
See what you really love.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:44.150
Do what you feel you have
some kind of connection to.

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:49.150
Create your own voice, your
own vision, your own style.

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.722
Taking creative risks is
what fashion is about.

00:01:53.722 --> 00:01:58.150
I'm Marc Jacobs, and
this is my MasterClass.

